# Required: the access code. A long random value (`openssl rand -base64 24`). The app shows only a lock screen until
# this code is entered, and the server refuses every request without it (and refuses everything if it is not set).
# For local development, put it in .env.local and type the same value into the lock screen.
APP_SECRET=
# Required: server-side key for the "Edit trip" / "Plan this trip" / "New trip" Claude calls.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional: the workspace ID (wrkspc_...) the key is meant to belong to. Requests are rejected if
# Anthropic reports that a different workspace served them. An API key is tied to one workspace, so
# this checks the key rather than choosing the workspace.
# ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=wrkspc_...
# Optional: override the model (defaults to claude-sonnet-5-5).
# CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# Optional: map tiles. Defaults to the public OpenStreetMap tile server (fine for light use).
# For real traffic use a tile provider and set its URL template and attribution.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_TILES=https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_ATTRIBUTION=© OpenStreetMap contributors

# Optional: sync trips between devices. A Redis database. On Vercel: Storage → Marketplace → Upstash Redis → connect it to the project, which sets
#    these two for you (Vercel KV used to be this). A database made directly on Upstash uses UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL
#    and UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN instead; either pair works.
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# Optional: forward booking emails into the app (see cloudflare/email-worker). A long random string that the
# Cloudflare worker sends with each email; set the same value there with `wrangler secret put INBOUND_SECRET`.
# Needs the database above, since the in-app inbox is behind the access code (APP_SECRET).
# INBOUND_SECRET=
